  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $175M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department awarded 818 contracts with an average award size of $214K. Obligations fell 99.8% year over year. The FY2027 to date total sits well below recent full fiscal year totals, which include $73.3B in FY26, $28.3B in FY25, $23.6B in FY24, $23.9B in FY23, and $20.8B in FY22. Contracting in FY2027 to date is concentrated in a few service categories and vendors: Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds leads NAICS categories with $44.8M, and ARDENT GROUP, LLC leads vendors with $44.8M. IT services categories such as Custom Computer Programming Services and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services also account for substantial shares, with $36.8M and $29.4M respectively. The FY2027 to date picture reflects partial-year obligations and a sharp year-over-year decline in spending.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are DHS's FY2027 to date contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $175M in FY2027 to date. The Department made 818 awards with an average award size of $214K. Obligations fell 99.8% year over year. Full fiscal year comparators include $73.3B in FY26 and $28.3B in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate DHS contracting in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds is the top NAICS category with $44.8M. Custom Computer Programming Services and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services follow with $36.8M and $29.4M. ARDENT GROUP, LLC is the top vendor with $44.8M, followed by ACENTRA HEALTH LLC with $29.4M and METROIBR JV LLC with $22.7M."
      }
    ]
  },
